# tools/al/ales_stereo_reverb_gate_env_witness.rish -- the stereo envelope gate: the reverb's GATED TAIL given a shaped edge, across a stereo master (lotus-audio).
#
# Chapter: the Six-Chapter double-seat, Chapter C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark lotus-audio - rung lotus-audio.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-111333_fill-ales203-lotus-stereo-reverb-gate-env.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye (lotus-audio -- the named-room stereo wet, run over the master unchanged); lotus/gate_env.rye (lotus-audio -- the
# attack/release envelope gate and its guards, run per channel); lotus/reverb_gate_env.rye (lotus-audio -- the mono envelope gate this mirrors per ear);
# lotus/stereo_reverb_gate.rye (lotus-audio -- the static stereo gate this contains as its instantaneous limit); lotus/pan.rye (the StereoClip);
# lotus/clock.rye (lotus-audio -- the sample clock); lotus/timeline.rye (lotus-audio -- the Clip each channel holds, its sample_max the gate's rail).
#
# lotus/stereo_reverb_gate_env.rye carries lotus-audio's shaped-edge gated tail across a stereo master -- the SAME time-following envelope gate over BOTH
# channels of a StereoClip, one shared threshold, ratio, and attack/release, the image held. It reverberates the master wet in place through lotus-audio's
# stereo_reverb_preset UNCHANGED, prechecks the threshold, ratio, and both coefficients (the SAME guards lotus-audio raises) BEFORE the wet is written so a
# bad gate leaves both channels DRY and balanced (atomic), then follow-gates each channel's wet with a fresh envelope and no cross-channel read -- the
# left ear follow-gates left, the right ear follow-gates right, so the image the preset held is held. It invents no new audio arithmetic. The selftest
# proves on both channels: at ratio_num == ratio_den the span equals stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte; for a firm ratio each channel equals
# stereo_reverb_preset then gate_follow on that channel byte for byte and each shaped-gated channel differs from its wet; with unit attack and unit
# release it equals lotus-audio's static stereo_reverb_gate byte for byte (the static gate is its zero-smoothing limit); each gated channel's total energy
# is strictly less than its wet's; the image is held (a centred master identical channel-to-channel, a stereo master distinct); the channels leave
# balanced and silence stays silence; and the faults forward atomic (a bad threshold BadThreshold, a bad ratio BadRatio, an illegal coefficient
# BadCoeff with both channels still dry, DurationTooLong, BadRange). Purely local -- one StereoClip, a validated clock; no network, no keys, no funds,
# no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_reverb_gate_env_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: Language EN — lotus-audio gave the MONO reverb its shaped-edge gated tail (a time-following envelope gate whose release holds the gate open over the decay, so the tail breathes rather than chops); a keeper mixing a STEREO master still had only the STATIC stereo gate (lotus-audio), the shaped edge stopped at mono exactly as the static gate did before lotus-audio carried it across. This rung is the thin twin lotus-audio named next: the SAME envelope gate, over BOTH channels of a StereoClip, one shared threshold, ratio, and attack/release, the image held — a clean composition of lotus-audio's stereo wet and lotus-audio's proven envelope gate run per ear."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: Style Radiant — the identity edge is stated positively and proven exact on both channels: at ratio_num == ratio_den the span equals stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte (a unit-ratio follow-gate is the un-gated stereo reverb); a larger ratio cuts the below-threshold tail harder on both ears, and a slower release holds the gate open longer over each ear's decay. The static stereo gate (lotus-audio) lives on as this rung's zero-smoothing limit: unit attack and unit release make each envelope the bare magnitude, so stereo_reverb_gate_env then equals stereo_reverb_gate byte for byte on both channels. The image is held — the left ear follow-gates left, the right ear follow-gates right, with a fresh envelope per ear and no cross-channel read."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: Lens TAME — one StereoClip of i16 PCM, a validated clock, and lotus-audio's fixed banks; NO new audio arithmetic — the gate is lotus-audio's proven envelope-following gate over the proven stereo wet, run per ear; StereoReverbGateEnvError = stereo_reverb_preset.StereoReverbPresetError || BadThreshold || BadRatio || BadCoeff, the gate's threshold, ratio, and both coefficients PRECHECKED before the wet is written (the same guards lotus-audio raises) so a bad gate leaves both channels dry and balanced (atomic), DurationTooLong / BadRange / BadThreshold / BadRatio / BadCoeff by name before any write; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device. A wet-tail stereo envelope gate; the attack/release are fractions per sample index."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate_env"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_gate_env.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate_env.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env line"

# This rung runs lotus-audio's stereo_reverb_preset over its public API for the wet -- re-prove the stereo named-room preset still stands green beside it.
let preset = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_preset && lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_preset selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-preset' && echo yes"]
assert (trim preset.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: the lotus-audio stereo named-room preset regressed under its envelope gate"

# And re-prove lotus-audio's mono envelope gate still stands green -- the rung this mirrors per ear.
let monoenv = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/reverb_gate_env.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/reverb_gate_env && lotus/bin/reverb_gate_env selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-reverb-gate-env' && echo yes"]
assert (trim monoenv.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: the lotus-audio mono envelope gate regressed beside its stereo twin"

# And re-prove lotus-audio's static stereo gate still stands green -- the instantaneous limit this rung equals.
let staticgate = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_gate.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate && lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-gate' && echo yes"]
assert (trim staticgate.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: the lotus-audio static stereo gate regressed beside its envelope gate"

say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: GREEN — the stereo envelope gate: the reverb's GATED TAIL given a shaped edge, across a stereo master. Reverberate the master wet in place through lotus-audio's stereo_reverb_preset unchanged, then follow-gate each channel's wet with lotus-audio's proven envelope gate at the same threshold, ratio, and attack/release — run per ear with a fresh envelope and no cross-channel read, ratio_num == ratio_den the identity, a larger ratio cutting the quiet tail harder, a slower release holding the gate open longer — no new audio arithmetic. Proven on both channels: at ratio_num == ratio_den exactly stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte; for a firm ratio each channel equals stereo_reverb_preset then gate_follow byte for byte and each shaped-gated channel differs from its wet; with unit attack and unit release it equals lotus-audio's static stereo_reverb_gate byte for byte; each gated channel's total energy is strictly less than its wet's; the image is held (a centred master identical channel-to-channel, a stereo master distinct); the channels leave balanced and silence stays silence; a bad threshold refuses BadThreshold, a bad ratio BadRatio, an illegal coefficient BadCoeff with both channels still dry, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving both channels untouched; the lotus-audio stereo preset, the lotus-audio mono envelope gate, and the lotus-audio static stereo gate stay GREEN beside it. The gate axis now stands whole for mono and stereo in both its static and shaped forms; a fresh reverb axis (width, freeze, or early/late balance) is next."
